>>>
>>
>> Crap! And what if "experts" are designated by the community?
>>
>
> The community that is not even able to grasp simple aspects of the grammar?
>

Hm... good point. Are you absolutely sure the community can't self-organize 
? In that case, any better idea to avoid current issues? I mean:

   1. Actual "experts" may be lead to an even more cluttered situation.
   2. The community is heterogeneous and cannot tell who are to be the 
   "meritant" (worthy) ones.

 

> Or maybe some kind of algorithm checking the "merit" of the user by 
>> scanning cor contributions and posted messages? Well, that last idea may be 
>> cumbersome, but...
>>
>
And about this? May we find a set of rules that can roughly "sort" user in 
a few groups? Maybe that would be imprecise and imperfect, but that may be 
better than nothing.

And about the submission protocol itself, any thoughts?

